[20.444221, "o", "\r\u001b[K`git log -p` shows commit history along with the patch (diff) introduced by each commit.\r\n\r\n- `git log` lists commits, newest first.\r\n- `-p` / `--patch` prints the file-by-file changes for every listed commit.\r\n\r\nUseful variants:\r\n\r\n```sh\r\ngit log -p -n 3          # patches for the latest 3 commits\r\ngit log -p -- path/to/file  # history and patches affecting one path\r\ngit log -p --author=Alice  # patches from matching author\r\ngit log -p main..feature   # commits reachable from feature but not main\r\n```\r\n\r\nPress `q` to exit the pager. Use `--stat` instead of `-p` for a compact per-commit file-change summary.\r\n"]
